      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "This study presents a scalable data-driven algorithm designed to efficiently address the",
      "bbox": [
        109.56700134277344,
        358.7457580566406,
        502.0179138183594,
        367.542724609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "challenging problem of reachability analysis. Analysis of cyber-physical systems (CPS)",
      "bbox": [
        109.92500305175781,
        370.7007751464844,
        503.22943115234375,
        379.49774169921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "relies typically on parametric physical models of dynamical systems. However, identify-",
      "bbox": [
        109.92500305175781,
        382.65576171875,
        503.7476806640625,
        391.4527282714844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ing parametric physical models for complex CPS is challenging due to their complexity,",
      "bbox": [
        109.92500305175781,
        394.6117858886719,
        503.4427795410156,
        403.40875244140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "uncertainty, and variability, often rendering them as black-box oracles. As an alternative,",
      "bbox": [
        109.92500305175781,
        406.5667724609375,
        503.46875,
        415.3637390136719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "one can treat these complex systems as black-box models and use trajectory data sampled",
      "bbox": [
        109.92500305175781,
        418.5217590332031,
        502.01873779296875,
        427.3187255859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "from the system (e.g., from high-fidelity simulators or the real system) along with machine",
      "bbox": [
        109.92500305175781,
        430.4767761230469,
        502.08453369140625,
        439.27374267578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "learning techniques to learn models that approximate the underlying dynamics. However,",
      "bbox": [
        109.92500305175781,
        442.4317626953125,
        503.4335632324219,
        451.2287292480469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "these machine learning models can be inaccurate, highlighting the need for statistical",
      "bbox": [
        109.92500305175781,
        454.3877868652344,
        502.0304870605469,
        463.18475341796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tools to quantify errors. Recent advancements in the field include the incorporation of",
      "bbox": [
        109.92500305175781,
        466.3427734375,
        502.0508117675781,
        475.1397399902344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "statistical uncertainty quantification tools such as conformal inference (CI) that can provide",
      "bbox": [
        109.92500305175781,
        478.2977600097656,
        502.060302734375,
        487.0947265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "probabilistic reachable sets with provable guarantees. Recent work has even highlighted",
      "bbox": [
        109.92500305175781,
        490.2527770996094,
        502.04046630859375,
        499.04974365234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the ability of these tools to address the case where the distribution of trajectories sampled",
      "bbox": [
        109.92500305175781,
        502.207763671875,
        502.0484313964844,
        511.0047302246094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "during training time are different from the distribution of trajectories encountered during",
      "bbox": [
        109.92500305175781,
        514.1627197265625,
        502.0712585449219,
        522.959716796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "deployment time. However, accounting for such distribution shifts typically results in",
      "bbox": [
        109.92500305175781,
        526.1187744140625,
        502.0710144042969,
        534.915771484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "more conservative guarantees. This is undesirable in practice and motivates us to present",
      "bbox": [
        109.92500305175781,
        538.07373046875,
        502.30096435546875,
        546.8707275390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "techniques that can reduce conservatism. Here, we propose a new approach that reduces",
      "bbox": [
        109.92500305175781,
        550.0287475585938,
        502.0015869140625,
        558.8257446289062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "conservatism and improves scalability by combining conformal inference with Principal",
      "bbox": [
        109.92500305175781,
        561.9837646484375,
        502.0608215332031,
        570.78076171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Component Analysis (PCA). We show the effectiveness of our technique on various case",
      "bbox": [
        109.92500305175781,
        573.938720703125,
        502.03033447265625,
        582.7357177734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "studies, including a 12-dimensional quadcopter and a 27-dimensional hybrid system known",
      "bbox": [
        109.92500305175781,
